Both branches pass the symbolic field-equation checks with different, precisely tuned values of \(\beta\). The curved Kantowski–Sachs branch has constant \(Y\) and exponentially growing \(X\); the flat Bianchi I branch has zero shear. Cases (b) and (c) close once the energy–temperature function is specified. Case (d) needs one pressure equation of state, \(p=P(\epsilon,n)\).
